{
 "milestones": [
  {
   "id": "m1",
   "title": "Add has_path function",
   "requests": [
    "R4"
   ],
   "requirement": "Add a has_path(obj, path) function that checks if an object has a specific attribute path (e.g., 'a.b.c') without raising AttributeError.",
   "observable": "has_path({'a': {'b': 1}}, 'a.b') is True; has_path({'a': 1}, 'a.b') is False; has_path(1, 'x') is False; has_path(None, '') is False.",
   "public_names": [
    "has_path"
   ],
   "requires": [],
   "why_requires": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "m2",
   "title": "Support dynamic exception in @reraise",
   "requests": [
    "R2"
   ],
   "requirement": "@reraise should accept a callable for the 'into' argument that returns the exception instance to raise, allowing dynamic exception construction.",
   "observable": "with reraise(ValueError, lambda: ValueError('dynamic msg'))(): pass raises ValueError with message 'dynamic msg'; with reraise(ValueError, TypeError)(): pass raises TypeError.",
   "public_names": [
    "reraise"
   ],
   "requires": [],
   "why_requires": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "m3",
   "title": "Unify memoize and cache invalidation API",
   "requests": [
    "R1"
   ],
   "requirement": "Ensure both @memoize and @cache decorated functions expose consistent invalidation methods: .invalidate(*args, **kwargs) and .invalidate_all(). Specifically add these to @memoize to match @cache's existing interface.",
   "observable": "dec = memoize()(lambda x: x); dec.invalidate(); dec.invalidate_all(); hasattr(dec, 'memory') is True; dec_cache = cache(60)(lambda x: x); dec_cache.invalidate(); dec_cache.invalidate_all(); hasattr(dec_cache, 'memory') is False.",
   "public_names": [
    "memoize",
    "cache"
   ],
   "requires": [],
   "why_requires": ""
  }
 ],
 "expected_causes": [
  "For m1: Developer might implement has_path using getattr with a default value, which would return the default instead of False if the attribute exists but is None or falsy, or fail to handle intermediate non-dict/non-object attributes correctly by raising an error instead of returning False.",
  "For m2: Developer might not realize 'into' can be a callable and only handle exception classes/instances, leading to incorrect instantiation or failure to support dynamic messages.",
  "For m3: Developer might incorrectly copy the implementation from cache which uses datetime/timedelta logic, whereas memoize uses a simple dict, or forget to add invalidate/invalidate_all to memoize wrapper."
 ],
 "verifier_plan": "Test m1 by creating nested dicts/objects and checking various paths including missing keys and non-dict intermediates. Test m2 by calling reraise with a lambda and verifying the raised exception type and message, and with a class to ensure backward compatibility. Test m3 by decorating a function with @memoize and @cache, calling them, then calling .invalidate() and .invalidate_all() and verifying the cache/memory state is cleared appropriately."
}
